# Skill: Agent Memory Architecture

Purpose:
  Engineering skill for designing and operating agent memory systems —
  the patterns behind SDDRA's 4-tier memory model. Use when reasoning
  about memory storage, retrieval, consolidation, or governance.

Owns: engineering/memory-architecture.sdd

Source: research round 3 r1 (2026-09-07) — Mem0, Letta, Zep/Graphiti,
  LangMem, Cognee, MemOS, A-MEM, OpenAI Dreaming, VMG; sources cited in
  .sdd/runtime/memory-model.sdd Phase 149 additions.

Patterns:
  tiered_memory:
    - working (context window) -> episodic (session) -> semantic (facts)
      -> procedural (skills) — separation by lifetime + write policy
    - hot/cold split: hot (>=50% recent reference) default-loaded; cold
      on-demand (90-day gate)
  write_paths:
    - hot path: critical + importance-rated (decisions) — explicit,
      immediate, auditable
    - background path: everything else — deferred consolidation
    - rule: decisions, not conversations
  supersession:
    - bi-temporal (t_valid/t_invalid/supersedes); invalidate, never delete
    - implicit conflicts trigger review, not silent coexistence
  retrieval:
    - fused additive score: semantic + keyword(BM25) + entity + recency
      decay + importance (recency ranks, never gates alone)
    - principal-scoped: no cross-project/agent bleed
  consolidation:
    - sleep-time triggers (end_of_task, step-count, compaction, idle);
      off-latency; may use stronger model
    - ratio discipline: ~100 events -> ~3 decisions + 1 skill candidate
  governance_primitives (VMG):
    - write authorization, provenance visibility, verified forgetting,
      principal-scoped retrieval, rollbackability (version chains)
  skill_crystallization:
    - repeated validated patterns promote to skill tier with provenance

AntiPatterns:
  - memory-as-RAG only (stateless retrieval misses staleness/identity)
  - delete on invalidation (destroys audit trail)
  - public benchmark chasing (LoCoMo audit: 6.4% wrong answer key)
  - context bloat: injecting full memories (progressive disclosure only)

Rules:
  [MA1] Apply patterns via .sdd/runtime/memory-model.sdd — this skill is
        the reasoning layer, the spec is authority.
  [MA2] Every memory design decision cites its pattern provenance.

